Certainly! Below is a simple HTML and CSS code snippet to create a minimalist homepage with placeholder navigation links for future experiments. This design is light and clean, focusing on simplicity.

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>Minimalist Homepage</title>
    <style>
        body {
            font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
            margin: 0;
            padding: 0;
            background-color: #f4f4f9;
            color: #333;
            display: flex;
            flex-direction: column;
            align-items: center;
            justify-content: center;
            height: 100vh;
        }

        header {
            margin-bottom: 50px;
        }

        nav {
            display: flex;
            gap: 20px;
        }

        a {
            text-decoration: none;
            color: #333;
            font-size: 18px;
            transition: color 0.3s;
        }

        a:hover {
            color: #007BFF;
        }

        .container {
            text-align: center;
        }

        h1 {
            font-size: 36px;
            margin-bottom: 20px;
        }

        p {
            font-size: 18px;
            color: #666;
        }
    </style>
</head>
<body>
    <header>
        <h1>Welcome to SpiritOS Experiments</h1>
    </header>
    <nav>
        <a href="#home">Home</a>
        <a href="#calculator">Calculator</a>
        <a href="#tarot">Tarot Deck Simulator</a>
        <a href="#weather">Weather App</a>
        <a href="#pong">Pong</a>
    </nav>
    <div class="container">
        <p>This is a minimalist homepage with placeholder navigation links for future experiments.</p>
    </div>
</body>
</html>
```

### Explanation:
- **HTML Structure**: The page includes a header with a title and a navigation bar with placeholder links for different experiments.
- **CSS Styling**: The styling is minimalistic, using a light background color and simple typography. Hover effects are added to the navigation links for better user interaction.
- **Responsive Design**: The layout is flexible and centered, making it suitable for various screen sizes.

You can expand upon this template by adding more functionality and content as you develop each experiment.
